Chapter: MutableSeq
  cites Codex chapter General

 Inside a let body a field assignment may precede the result: each
 `<assign> in <rest>` sequences the in-place write before the rest. With
 a `mutable T` parameter this is the natural way to fill in a record's
 fields and then read them back.

Section: Definitions

  mutable Box = record {
    n : Integer,
    m : Integer
  }

  tally : mutable Box -> Text
  tally (b) =
    let x = b
    in x.n = x.n + 5
    in x.m = x.m + x.n
    in "n=" & show (x.n) & " m=" & show (x.m)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (tally (Box { n = 0, m = 1 }))
  end
